Polymorphism Trap
class A {
    void show(Object obj) {
        System.out.println("Object");
    }
}

class B extends A {

    void show(String str) {
        System.out.println("String");
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        A obj = new B();

        obj.show("Hello");
    }
}




=====================================output===================================
Compiler checks methods available in class A.

show(Object obj)
exists.

Compiler binds call to:
show(Object)

Now runtime looks for an overridden version.
B has: show(String)

This is overloading, not overriding.

No override exists.

Therefore:
             Object

Output:    Object
